msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid "Today, we announce the availability of Quarkus 1.13.0.Final."
msgstr ""

msgid "This release brings several new features:"
msgstr ""

msgid "DevServices simplifies testing with containers."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenTelemetry is now supported via two new extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes Service Binding simplifies the deployment on Kubernetes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We introduced a new MicroProfile REST Client based on RESTEasy Reactive."
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jacoco` can generate your test coverage reports."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"And as usual its fair share of bugfixes and small improvements all over the "
"place."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Eager to migrate your existing applications? Here is https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-1.13[our migration guide for 1.13]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Zero Config Setup with DevServices"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Quarkus, our main goal is to make developer lives easier and bring back "
"developer joy.\n"
"In 1.13, we added a new element to the (not so secret) Quarkus recipe: "
"DevServices."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When starting dev mode (live reload), we are now able to automatically start "
"containers for your tests and you don't even need to configure anything:\n"
"the container is automatically wired to the Quarkus dev mode configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For instance, if you're developing a PostgreSQL-based application, as soon "
"as you have the PostgreSQL JDBC extension in your pom, a container will be "
"started for testing using Testcontainers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You only need to define your configuration for production with the `%prod.` "
"prefix.\n"
"The dev mode one is taken care of."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You will find all the details about this new feature in the link:/guides/"
"datasource#devservices-configuration-free-databases[Datasource guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenTelemetry Extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://opentelemetry.io/[OpenTelemetry] project from the https://www."
"cncf.io[Cloud Native Computing Foundation] is an initiative to merge the "
"OpenTracing and OpenCensus projects to provide a common project for all "
"telemetry. Tracing is the first piece of OpenTelemetry which GA'd in the "
"last month, metrics and logging are still under development."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 1.13 introduces a new extension for OpenTelemetry called `quarkus-"
"opentelemetry` which offers the ability to trace requests. For exporting "
"traces to a Jaeger collector, use the `quarkus-opentelemetry-exporter-"
"jaeger` extension which depends on `quarkus-opentelemetry`.\n"
"With this initial version, traces are available in JAX-RS Resource methods, "
"REST Client, and Reactive Messaging with Kafka. Further integrations with "
"other extensions will come in future releases, as well as a guide and "
"quickstart."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes Service Binding"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus supports binding services to applications via the https://github.com/"
"k8s-service-bindings/spec[Service Binding Specification for Kubernetes].\n"
"Specifically Quarkus implements the https://github.com/k8s-service-bindings/"
"spec#application-projection[Application Projection] part of the "
"specification, thus allowing\n"
"applications running in appropriately configured Kubernetes clusters to "
"consume services (such as a Database or a Broker) without the need for user "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "Currently, the following Quarkus extensions support this feature:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jdbc-mariadb`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jdbc-mssql`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jdbc-mysql`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jdbc-postgresql`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-kafka-client`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-smallrye-reactive-messaging-kafka`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This list of extensions will grow as more services with supported bindings "
"become available on Kubernetes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable Service Binding support, in addition to one of the currently "
"supported extensions, the `quarkus-kubernetes-service-binding` extension "
"needs to be added to the application dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Everything you need to know about it is detailed in the link:/guides/"
"deploying-to-kubernetes#service-binding[Kubernetes guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile REST Client based on RESTEasy Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We are continuing to enrich the RESTEasy Reactive experience and, this time, "
"it's on the REST Client front.\n"
"A new RESTEasy Reactive-based REST Client extension `quarkus-rest-client-"
"reactive` is present in Quarkus 1.13."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that RESTEasy Reactive can be used for reactive but also for "
"traditional blocking workloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "Vert.x based Websockets"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Until now, if you wanted websockets support in your applications, you had to "
"switch to Undertow."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 1.13 introduces a pure-Vert.x-based Websockets extension called "
"`quarkus-websockets`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Test Coverage Reports"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Given the way Quarkus is architected, it was not as easy as it should be to "
"generate test coverage reports with Jacoco."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 1.13 comes with `quarkus-jacoco` which will automatically generate "
"your test coverage reports. And it does not require any Maven setup anymore. "
"More about this in link:/guides/tests-with-coverage[our updated guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "@QuarkusIntegrationTest"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@QuarkusIntegrationTest` is the natural evolution of `@NativeImageTest` "
"(which is still supported) and can be used to launch and test the artifact "
"produced by the Quarkus build, and supports testing a jar (of all types), a "
"native binary or container-image.\n"
"For more information see link:https://quarkus.io/guides/getting-started-"
"testing#quarkus-integration-test[this] part of the documentation and the "
"Javadoc of the annotation itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full Changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelogs of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/1.13.0.CR1[1.13.0.CR1], and https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/releases/tag/1.13.0.Final[1.13.0.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

msgid "ADOPTERS.md"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To share stories about Quarkus usage, we added https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/blob/master/ADOPTERS.md[an `ADOPTERS.md` file] at the root of the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are using Quarkus and would like to be interviewed on our blog or "
"simply added to this file, please contact us and we will be happy to oblige."
msgstr ""

